   "evidence": "`ofExcl_Pq/Dq/Q2/t/x` at lines 166\u2013204 are the only lemmas about `ofExcl`; grep for `ofExcl_xi`, `ofExcl_beta`, `ofExcl_absT` in the PR returns nothing. `def x`/`xi`/`beta`/`absT` at lines 86, 92, 98, 105 sit under `public section` (line 37) with no `@[expose]`, unlike `Exclusive/Kinematics/Basic.lean:18` which is `@[expose] public section`.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Scattering/DIS/Diffractive/Kinematics.lean",
   "fix": "Add `@[simp] theorem ofExcl_xi \u2026 : (ofExcl g K hPq hDq hQ2 ht).xi = -g K.delta K.q / g K.p K.q`, `@[simp] theorem ofExcl_beta \u2026 = K.Q2 g / (2 * -g K.delta K.q)` and `@[simp] theorem ofExcl_absT \u2026 = -K.tMom g`, each provable by `rw [xi_def, ofExcl_Dq, ofExcl_Pq]` and analogues, so all four derived quantities of the bridge are characterised uniformly.",
   "issue": "`ofExcl` is characterised on `Pq/Dq/Q2/t` and on `x` (`ofExcl_x`, line 199) but not on the other operations in scope: there is no `ofExcl_xi`, `ofExcl_beta` or `ofExcl_absT`. Those are the Layer 0.1 definitions of \u03be and \u03b2 in terms of momenta that Layer 0.2\u20130.3 (`x \u2264 \u03be \u2264 1`, `t \u2264 0` on the region, the gap\u2013\u03be bound) will state about real events. The file is `public section` without `@[expose]`, so the bodies of `xi`/`beta`/`absT` are unavailable downstream, and `xi_def`/`beta_def`/`absT_eq_neg_t` (lines 95, 101, 108) are not `@[simp]`: a consumer must hand-rewrite with `_def` before the `ofExcl_*` field lemmas can fire. Worse, `ofExcl_x` *is* `@[simp]`, so `simp` rewrites `(ofExcl \u2026).x` to `K.toDisKinematics.xBj g` while leaving `(ofExcl \u2026).xi * (ofExcl \u2026).beta` untouched, breaking the file's own identity `x_eq_xi_mul_beta` (line 134) on the bridge.",
   "line": 199
  }
